From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] grt: page a backed grid out before the routes are
 converted
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Global route peaks while it converts and saves the routes, when the grid
(the 2D and 3D edges and the capacity per layer) is not read. With
-backing_file the grid is now written to its file and its pages freed
there, and read back as it is next touched: the congestion report and
incremental routing read it again.

Only unmapping a dirty page of a shared file mapping (MADV_PAGEOUT
alone) leaves it in memory until the kernel writes it back: on a 512 MB
test mapping the cgroup still held 499 MB after the call. msync first,
then MADV_PAGEOUT, freed it at once: 3 MB held, 1.6 s for the write.
Without -backing_file nothing changes.

Carried in bazel-orfs for OpenROAD#12075, not upstreamed; retires with
the //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
---
 src/grt/src/fastroute/include/FileBacking.h |  4 ++++
 src/grt/src/fastroute/src/FastRoute.cpp     |  4 ++++
 src/grt/src/fastroute/src/FileBacking.cpp   | 13 +++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/grt/src/fastroute/include/FileBacking.h b/src/grt/src/fastroute/include/FileBacking.h
index eb5d248eb6..158270e41f 100644
--- a/src/grt/src/fastroute/include/FileBacking.h
+++ b/src/grt/src/fastroute/include/FileBacking.h
@@ -34,6 +34,10 @@ class FileBacking
   // allocator can reuse the addresses as ordinary memory and nothing more
   // is written to the file.
   void release();
+  // Writes the mapped ranges to the file and frees their pages now; they
+  // are read back as they are touched. A dirty page only unmapped would stay
+  // in memory until written back, so the ranges are synced first.
+  void pageOut();
 
   static size_t pageSlack();
 
diff --git a/src/grt/src/fastroute/src/FastRoute.cpp b/src/grt/src/fastroute/src/FastRoute.cpp
index 8e0f9c9d02..cc40411075 100644
--- a/src/grt/src/fastroute/src/FastRoute.cpp
+++ b/src/grt/src/fastroute/src/FastRoute.cpp
@@ -2822,6 +2822,10 @@ NetRouteMap FastRouteCore::run()
     }
   }
 
+  // The grid is not read while the routes are converted and saved, where
+  // global route peaks: with a backing file it is written out and freed,
+  // and read back as it is next touched.
+  backing_.pageOut();
   NetRouteMap routes = getRoutes();
   net_ids_.clear();
   return routes;
diff --git a/src/grt/src/fastroute/src/FileBacking.cpp b/src/grt/src/fastroute/src/FileBacking.cpp
index ca999b308e..9a8263b694 100644
--- a/src/grt/src/fastroute/src/FileBacking.cpp
+++ b/src/grt/src/fastroute/src/FileBacking.cpp
@@ -15,6 +15,11 @@
 
 #include "utl/Logger.h"
 
+// Linux 5.4; older system headers lack it, older kernels refuse it.
+#ifndef MADV_PAGEOUT
+#define MADV_PAGEOUT 21
+#endif
+
 namespace grt {
 
 void FileBacking::reserve(utl::Logger* logger,
@@ -115,6 +120,14 @@ void FileBacking::release()
   fd_ = -1;
 }
 
+void FileBacking::pageOut()
+{
+  for (const Range& range : ranges_) {
+    msync(range.data, range.len, MS_SYNC);
+    madvise(range.data, range.len, MADV_PAGEOUT);
+  }
+}
+
 size_t FileBacking::pageSlack()
 {
   return 2 * sysconf(_SC_PAGESIZE);
-- 
